# Code Quality Verification

Every code change must pass **Prettier**, **ESLint**, and **TypeScript** before done. Read config in the repo; do not guess rules.

## Config locations

| Tool | File |
|---|---|
| Prettier | `.prettierrc` |
| ESLint | `eslint.config.js` |
| TypeScript (app) | `tsconfig.app.json` |
| TypeScript (node scripts) | `tsconfig.node.json` |
| Vitest | `vitest.config.ts` (if present) or `vite.config.ts` |

## After edits

Run on **touched areas** unless the change is broad:

```bash
pnpm format          # or prettier --write on touched paths
pnpm lint:fix
pnpm build           # tsc --noEmit + vite build
pnpm test            # when logic changed; run affected tests if possible
```

Then `ReadLints` on changed files. Re-run until clean.

**Broad changes:** full `pnpm lint`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm test`.

Do not mass-reformat unrelated files in feature work. Format/lint only what you touch.

## Unrelated files

Do not reorder imports or apply style-only fixes on files out of scope for the current task, even if the linter flags them.

| Situation | Do |
|---|---|
| File out of scope | Leave as-is |
| Brief touch (re-export) | Change only what the task requires |
| `lint:fix` touched unrelated paths | Revert those hunks |
| File in scope and edited | Format/lint that file |

## Do not

- Fix import order in unrelated files
- Skip reading eslint/prettier/tsconfig before editing unfamiliar areas
- Use `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly requests it
- Disable ESLint or `@ts-ignore` without fixing root cause
- Edit `public/data/` generated JSON by hand (use `pnpm run fetch-data` / rebuild scripts)
